  "notes": "An ichidan (る) verb. The passive form {閉|と}じ{込|こ}められる is very common, describing being trapped or confined against one's will.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ～を～に{閉|と}じ{込|こ}める (to shut ~ in ~)\n- ～に{閉|と}じ{込|こ}められる (to be trapped/confined in ~)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {部屋|へや}に{閉|と}じ{込|こ}める (to lock in a room)\n- {心|こころ}に{閉|と}じ{込|こ}める (to lock away in one's heart)\n- {雪|ゆき}で{閉|と}じ{込|こ}められる (to be snowed in)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\nThe intransitive counterpart is {閉|と}じこもる (to shut oneself in; to become a recluse).",
